## Theme Mappings

{THEME_MAPPINGS_SECTION}

## Using This Style

To generate UI matching this style:

1. **Always reference semantic tokens** in your component styles (e.g., `color.action.primary`, not `color.blue.500`)
2. **Primitive tokens** are raw materials — access them only through semantic aliases
3. **Component tokens** are overrides — use only when a component has a genuinely independent value
4. **Check theme mappings** — the same semantic token resolves to different primitives in light vs dark mode

### Do's and Don'ts

| Do ✅ | Don't ❌ |
|-------|---------|
| `background: var(--color-bg-surface)` | `background: #FFFFFF` (hardcoded) |
| `background: var(--color-action-primary)` | `background: var(--color-blue-500)` (bypassing semantic layer) |
| Create new semantic token if role is missing | Create component token when semantic token would work |
| Check light AND dark theme mappings | Assume one theme's value works for the other |

